{"type":"standard","title":"Bruce Blakeman","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Bruce Blakeman</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q110712423","titles":{"canonical":"Bruce_Blakeman","normalized":"Bruce Blakeman","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Bruce Blakeman</span></span>"},"pageid":29509870,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Blakeman_Profile_Picture.jpg/330px-Blakeman_Profile_Picture.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":381},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fe/Blakeman_Profile_Picture.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":675,"height":780},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1378604796","tid":"94c7ecbb-c076-11f1-bf29-a02e668039e9","timestamp":"2026-10-05T04:38:16Z","description":"American politician (born 1955)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce_Blakeman","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce_Blakeman?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce_Blakeman?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Bruce_Blakeman"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce_Blakeman","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Bruce_Blakeman","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce_Blakeman?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Bruce_Blakeman"}},"extract":"Bruce Arthur Blakeman is an American attorney and politician currently serving as the 10th county executive of Nassau County, New York. A Republican, Blakeman was first elected in 2021, defeating Democratic incumbent Laura Curran and becoming the county's first Jewish county executive. He previously served as a commissioner for the New York-New Jersey Port Authority, as well as a Nassau County legislator and Hempstead town councilman. He is the Republican nominee in the 2026 New York gubernatorial election.","extract_html":"<p><b>Bruce Arthur Blakeman</b> is an American attorney and politician currently serving as the 10th county executive of Nassau County, New York. A Republican, Blakeman was first elected in 2021, defeating Democratic incumbent Laura Curran and becoming the county's first Jewish county executive. He previously served as a commissioner for the New York-New Jersey Port Authority, as well as a Nassau County legislator and Hempstead town councilman. He is the Republican nominee in the 2026 New York gubernatorial election.</p>"}